red later", "Evidence ready for licence applications, audits and supplier questions"], "tags": ["governance", "platform", "kubernetes"], "keywords": ["GPU cloud export controls", "US AI chip licence Malaysia", "BIS rule remote access AI chips", "Malaysia Strategic Trade Act AI chips", "MITI AI chip permit", "know your customer compute", "Kueue GPU admission", "data centre compliance Malaysia", "AI infrastructure regulation Southeast Asia", "fractional CTO Malaysia"], "faq": [["What changed for GPU clouds in Malaysia in November 2026?", "Reporting says the US Commerce Department issued a rule requiring licences for advanced AI chips going to Malaysia and four other countries and targeting remote access to controlled chips through data centres in third countries. This adds to Malaysia's 2025 requirement for permits to export, transship or transit US-origin high-performance AI chips."], ["What is know-your-customer for compute?", "Screening and verifying who uses compute capacity, including who ultimately owns or controls the customer, and keeping that knowledge current as customers, users and workloads change."], ["How can a Kubernetes platform enforce compliance for GPU access?", "By tying GPU quota and job admission to each tenant's compliance status, so jobs from tenants whose checks are incomplete or have lapsed wait or are refused, and by logging every job and access with the identity behind it."]], "related": ["/ai-architect/", "/fractional-cto-singapore/", "/regions/"], "citations": [{"title": "US Dep't of Commerce issues rule to restrict remote access to advanced AI chips", "url": "https://www.datacenterdynamics.com/en/news/us-dept-of-commerce-issues-rule-to-restrict-remote-access-to-advanced-ai-chips/", "publisher": "DCD", "date": "Nov 2026"}, {"title": "Commerce Department moves to close AI chip loophole", "url": "https://www.nextgov.com/artificial-intelligence/2026/11/commerce-department-moves-close-ai-chip-loophole/417255/", "publisher": "Nextgov/FCW", "da